---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Navbar from '../../components/Navbar.astro';
import Footer from '../../components/Footer.astro';

const title = 'Wix vs Custom Website: Which Is Right for Your Business?';
const description = 'The honest truth about website builders vs custom development. When Wix is enough, when it is not, and how to make the right choice.';
---

<Layout title={title} description={description}>
  <Navbar />
  <article class="blog-post">
    <div class="hero-bg">
      <div class="gradient-blob blob-1"></div>
      <div class="gradient-blob blob-2"></div>
    </div>
    <div class="container">
      <header class="post-header reveal">
        <div class="post-meta">
          <span class="post-category">Web Design</span>
          <span class="post-date">May 2026 · 6 min read</span>
        </div>
        <h1 class="post-title">Wix vs Custom Website: Which Is Right for Your Business?</h1>
        <p class="post-excerpt">The honest truth about website builders vs custom development. When Wix is enough, when it is not, and how to make the right choice for your stage of business.</p>
      </header>
      <div class="post-content reveal">
        <p class="lead">You have a business to run. You need a website. And now you are stuck in the endless debate: Wix or custom? Here is the answer no one else will give you.</p>

        <h2>When Wix (or Squarespace) Is Perfectly Fine</h2>
        <p>Let us be honest — website builders have come a long way. For certain use cases, they are genuinely good enough:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>You need a simple portfolio or brochure site</li>
          <li>You have zero budget and need something live today</li>
          <li>You enjoy tinkering and have time to learn</li>
          <li>Your business does not depend on website leads</li>
          <li>You are pre-revenue and validating an idea</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Wix and Squarespace are great tools. They let non-technical people build decent-looking sites quickly. But they have hard limits — and those limits cost you money.</p>

        <h2>The Hidden Problems With Website Builders</h2>
        <h3>1. Speed Kills Conversions</h3>
        <p>Wix sites average 4–8 second load times. Google says 53% of mobile visitors leave if a page takes longer than 3 seconds. That is not a statistic — that is half your potential customers, gone.</p>

        <h3>2. SEO Limitations</h3>
        <p>Website builders have gotten better at SEO, but they still lag behind custom builds. You cannot fully control technical SEO elements, structured data, or page speed — all major ranking factors.</p>

        <h3>3. Template Trap</h3>
        <p>Your site looks like 10,000 other businesses. That is not branding — that is camouflage. In competitive markets, blending in is the same as being invisible.</p>

        <h3>4. Platform Lock-In</h3>
        <p>Your entire business is on Wix servers. If they raise prices, change features, or go down, you have zero control. Moving off the platform often means rebuilding from scratch.</p>

        <h2>When You Need a Custom Website</h2>
        <p>Custom development is not about prestige. It is about performance. You need a custom site when:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Your website is a primary lead source</li>
          <li>You compete in a market where every advantage matters</li>
          <li>You need specific functionality (booking, calculators, integrations)</li>
          <li>You want full control over SEO and performance</li>
          <li>You plan to scale and need a foundation that grows with you</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>The Real Cost Comparison</h2>
        <p>Let us look at 2 years of ownership:</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Wix Business:</strong> $30/mo × 24 months = $720. Plus your time. Plus lost leads from slow speed and poor SEO.</li>
          <li><strong>Custom Build:</strong> $4,500 upfront. $0/month if you self-host. Better performance, better SEO, more leads.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>The custom site pays for itself if it generates even one extra client per month.</p>

        <h2>The Hybrid Approach</h2>
        <p>There is a middle ground. Start with a builder to validate your business. Once you have revenue and know your website needs to perform, invest in a custom build. Many of our clients started on Wix and came to us when they outgrew it.</p>

        <div class="cta-box">
          <h3>Not Sure Which Path Is Right?</h3>
          <p>Book a free call and we will help you figure out what makes sense for your stage and budget. No upsell, just honest advice.</p>
          <a href="https://calendly.com/getonwardcraft/30min" class="cta-button">Get Free Advice</a>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="post-footer reveal">
        <div class="post-tags"><span>Web Design</span><span>Wix</span><span>Small Business</span></div>
        <a href="/blog" class="back-link"><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><path d="M19 12H5"/><path d="M12 19l-7-7 7-7"/></svg>Back to Blog</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </article>
  <Footer />
</Layout>

<style>
  .blog-post { padding: 140px 0 80px; position: relative; overflow: hidden; background: var(--bg-primary); min-height: 100vh; }
  .hero-bg { position: absolute; inset: 0; overflow: hidden; }
  .gradient-blob { position: absolute; border-radius: 50%; filter: blur(120px); opacity: 0.3; }
  .blob-1 { width: 400px; height: 400px; background: radial-gradient(circle, rgba(59,130,246,0.3), transparent 70%); top: 5%; right: -10%; }
  .blob-2 { width: 300px; height: 300px; background: radial-gradient(circle, rgba(139,92,246,0.25), transparent 70%); bottom: 20%; left: -5%; }
  .post-header { position: relative; z-index: 1; max-width: 800px; margin: 0 auto 60px; text-align: center; }
  .post-meta { display: flex; justify-content: center; gap: 16px; margin-bottom: 24px; flex-wrap: wrap; }
  .post-category { font-size: 13px; font-weight: 600; color: var(--accent-primary); text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.06em; }
  .post-date { font-size: 13px; color: var(--text-muted); }
  .post-title { font-size: clamp(32px, 5vw, 52px); font-weight: 700; line-height: 1.1; margin-bottom: 20px; }
  .post-excerpt { font-size: 18px; color: var(--text-secondary); line-height: 1.7; max-width: 640px; margin: 0 auto; }
  .post-content { position: relative; z-index: 1; max-width: 720px; margin: 0 auto; }
  .post-content .lead { font-size: 20px; color: var(--text-primary); line-height: 1.7; margin-bottom: 40px; }
  .post-content h2 { font-size: 28px; font-weight: 700; margin: 48px 0 20px; color: var(--text-primary); }
  .post-content h3 { font-size: 20px; font-weight: 700; margin: 32px 0 12px; color: var(--text-primary); }
  .post-content p { font-size: 16px; color: var(--text-secondary); line-height: 1.8; margin-bottom: 20px; }
  .post-content ul, .post-content ol { margin: 0 0 24px 24px; }
  .post-content li { font-size: 16px; color: var(--text-secondary); line-height: 1.8; margin-bottom: 10px; }
  .post-content li strong { color: var(--text-primary); }
  .cta-box { background: linear-gradient(180deg, rgba(59,130,246,0.08) 0%, rgba(17,24,39,0.5) 100%); border: 1px solid rgba(59,130,246,0.2); border-radius: var(--radius-xl); padding: 40px; margin: 40px 0; text-align: center; }
  .cta-box h3 { font-size: 22px; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 12px; color: var(--text-primary); }
  .cta-box p { font-size: 16px; color: var(--text-secondary); line-height: 1.7; margin-bottom: 24px; }
  .cta-button { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 10px; padding: 16px 32px; background: var(--accent-primary); color: white; font-size: 15px; font-weight: 600; border-radius: var(--radius-md); transition: all 0.35s var(--transition); box-shadow: 0 4px 24px rgba(59,130,246,0.3); }
  .cta-button:hover { transform: translateY(-2px); box-shadow: 0 8px 32px rgba(59,130,246,0.4); }
  .post-footer { max-width: 720px; margin: 60px auto 0; padding-top: 40px; border-top: 1px solid var(--border); display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 20px; }
  .post-tags { display: flex; gap: 10px; flex-wrap: wrap; }
  .post-tags span { font-size: 13px; color: var(--text-muted); padding: 6px 14px; background: rgba(255,255,255,0.04); border-radius: 100px; }
  .back-link { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 8px; font-size: 14px; font-weight: 600; color: var(--accent-primary); transition: gap 0.3s; }
  .back-link:hover { gap: 12px; }
  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .blog-post { padding: 120px 0 60px; }
    .post-title { font-size: 28px; }
    .post-content .lead { font-size: 18px; }
    .post-content h2 { font-size: 24px; }
    .cta-box { padding: 28px 24px; }
    .gradient-blob { display: none; }
  }
</style>